# The submission tree is packaged byte-for-byte (see _package.py) and runs on
# Linux in the platform container. So the checkout has to be LF on every
# platform: with only `core.autocrlf=true` and no .gitattributes, git rewrites
# the working tree to CRLF on checkout, and the zip built from that tree no
# longer matches the committed one - the artifact stops being reproducible.
#
# `eol=lf` here pins both the index and the checkout, so the packaged bytes no
# longer depend on who cloned the repo or on their autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers, should any ever appear.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never let git touch these.
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
